{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## STATUS SNAPSHOT for handoff — 13/13 ACs met, 0 uncertified, 3 open children\n\n### The epic's own criteria: COMPLETE\n\nAll 13 acceptance criteria are met. **AC4 is ATTESTED** (operator, 2026-08-04) on harness run\n**30933704255** at `f70e5d2101`, with both halves of the bidirectional claim carried by dedicated cells\nthat PASSED:\n\n    test_a_dc_issue_reaches_the_local_store_inbound      — DC issue -> local store, inbound pass\n    test_a_local_edit_reaches_the_dc_issue_outbound      — local edit -> DC issue, outbound pass\n\n\"Zero unhandled exceptions\" is asserted inside those cells (`\"Traceback\" not in cp.stderr`), not\ninferred. Re-confirmed on run 30944241768 at `b868ea914`.\n\n### Certification: 0 uncertified descendants\n\nWas 2. `0059` was resolved by the disposition-attestation fix the operator ruled on\n([rebar:738a-376e-4829-42ca], Gerrit 1378 merged) — a duplicate-closed child now mints an honest\n`DISPOSITION` attestation instead of withholding the parent's signature. `b586` was resolved by\nre-parenting its orphaned children (see below).\n\n50 descendants; 45 closed, 3 in progress.\n\n### The 3 open children, and exactly what each waits on\n\n**`2e47`** — vocabularies. Four findings triaged; the label finding was **REFUTED by measurement** (DC\naccepts a 255-char label; the capability map's req-0071/0072/0073 does not reproduce — retracted in\nGerrit 1389). Two criteria wait on **harness run 30951453979** (dispatched, `d394a7052`) to emit the\n`[2e47-issue-type-evidence]` line that a bug of mine previously swallowed (fixed in 1390). If the run\nshows project-scoped issue-type name uniqueness, both criteria are met and it closes.\n\n**`3b5f`** — the dead `(inbound, probe)` chain. Plan is written and carries a signed PASS plan-review\nattestation; a subagent is implementing it. Decision recorded across DECISION-3B5F-A/B/C: **re-home, not\nwire-or-delete** — delete the dead legacy arm, and under the operator's \"never resurrect\" ruling REMOVE\nthe resurrection implementation rather than orphan it, plus a tombstone guard for the EXISTING\neventual-resurrection path (measured: 3 confirmed 404s retire the binding, the ticket goes unbound, and\n`outbound_differ.py:502-513` re-creates it).\n\n**`b586`** — BLOCKED on [rebar:df3a-5a7a-01e5-43f6], not on its own merits. All criteria checked, fresh\nPASS plan-review attestation, `child_closure_findings` reports 0 blocking / 0 uncertified. The close is\nrefused because the completion verifier returns a dependency-link record where a `CompletionVerdict`\nbelongs. Deliberately left `in_progress` rather than `--force-close`d, since a forced close is the\nunattested state this epic spent the cycle removing. A `/rebar-debug` subagent is root-causing it.\n\n### Landed this session: 12 changes, all `Verified +1` + `LLM-Review +1`\n\n    1370 d582  collision-free rekey target        1381 2e47  assert issue-type names unambiguous\n    1371 275e  non-admin app-properties probe     1387 9790  wait for Epic fields, not serverInfo\n    1372 59b2  let the vacuous assertions fail    1388 6a81  unblock recheck-review once attested\n    1373 4b9e  keep probe evidence on setup fail  1389 2e47  retract the label-ceiling mismatch\n    1375 2e47  vocabulary decisions as data       1390 2e47  fix the issue-type evidence line\n    1378 738a  attest a disposition close         1380 2bc7  guard the last two shared-key loaders\n\nClosed and certified this session: `0059`, `2bc7`, `d582`, `275e`, `59b2`."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785878345989877001,"uuid":"e8f2928f-3c33-4edf-9467-ec27090f153a"}